// Top-p (nucleus) renormalisation of dense row probabilities.
//
// Per row: c = max{v : S(v) >= p}, with S(v) the float64 sum of row entries
// >= v; output is x / S(c) for x >= c, else 0.
//
// One block per row, phases separated by block barriers:
//   A  sum histogram over the raw float bit pattern. A bin is 2"'^18 patterns
//      wide (~2% in value): fine enough to keep shared-atomic pressure low,
//      coarse enough to bracket the cutoff to within a bin.
//   B  descending walk of that histogram -> centre bin, plus the bin indices
//      where the sum crosses p.
//   C  one pass over the row: exact float64 sum above the centre bin'"'s top edge
//      and staging of the three bins around it. The staged entries are enough
//      to pin the crossing bin and the cutoff exactly; the walk in B only has
//      to be accurate to a bin, which float32 bin sums are.
//   D  shared-memory descents of the bracket down to a single float pattern.
//   E  elementwise normalised write.
//
// Non-negative floats are ordered by their bit pattern, so all value
// comparisons here are unsigned integer compares of patterns.

